<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" pages="22">
  <diagram id="p1" name="1 . Lifecycle and Requirements">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1410" dy="638" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1160" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p1_t" parent="1" style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" value="FINZORR.AI — AI Product Lifecycle &amp; Requirements. Multi-tenant AI financial assistant, LIVE in production at finzorr.ai. Green = built &amp; running today, amber dashed = planned / identified gap." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="26" width="1660" x="30" y="12" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s1" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="1. Business Problem&#xa;General-purpose AI assistant (ChatGPT-style: chat, documents, memory, tools) — Indian NSE/BSE stock-market finance as the first vertical (screening, fundamentals Q&amp;A, portfolio analysis). Multi-tenant, live at finzorr.ai. $0-marginal-cost policy: free-tier LLM providers only." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="112" width="290" x="50" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s2" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="2. Requirements&#xa;Functional + Non-Functional requirements captured before any model or architecture decisions (panels →)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="290" x="50" y="194" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s3" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="3. AI Feasibility&#xa;Conversational + document + finance-Q&amp;A use cases fit GenAI well; a free-tier LLM provider chain was judged sufficient to hit the $0-marginal-cost target." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="290" x="50" y="276" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s4" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="4. Model / Provider Selection&#xa;Outcome: a free-tier LLM provider chain (primary + fallback) wired through app/infrastructure/llm — the concrete mechanism behind the $0-marginal-cost policy." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="290" x="50" y="358" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s5" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="5. Architecture&#xa;5-layer backend: app/domain/ (pure business logic) → app/specialists/ (7 LangGraph nodes, Specialist Protocol) → app/infrastructure/ (Postgres/Redis/Qdrant/LLM adapters) → app/orchestration/ (graph, routing, turn lifecycle) → app/interface/ (FastAPI + WebSocket). Dependency is strictly one-directional: interface depends down through orchestration → specialists → infrastructure → domain, never the reverse." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="150" width="290" x="50" y="440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s6" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="6. Development&#xa;LangGraph 1.2.x StateGraph · AsyncPostgresSaver checkpointer · guard/injection-defense patterns · versioned prompt registry (AgentPrompt objects)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="80" width="290" x="50" y="602" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s7" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="7. Evaluation&#xa;Deterministic, CI-gated suites: routing_eval · injection_eval · plan_eval · rag_eval · grounded_eval. scripts/release_gate.sh chains them as the pre-release gate (numbers →)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="86" width="290" x="50" y="694" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s8" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="8. Deployment — LIVE&#xa;OVH dedicated server, 6 Docker containers (api / postgres+pgvector / redis / qdrant / ollama / cloudflared). Cloudflare Tunnel (outbound-only ingress) + Cloudflare Pages (frontend, via Wrangler CLI). Self-hosted GitHub Actions runner on the server for SSH-less CD." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="128" width="290" x="50" y="792" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s9" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="9. Monitoring&#xa;Opt-in LangSmith tracing (default off) · structured logs · scripts/drift_watch.py (daily eval regression alerting) · scripts/trace_health_watch.py (live degraded/suspicious tag-rate alerting)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="98" width="290" x="50" y="932" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_s10" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" value="10. Continuous Improvement&#xa;👍/👎 feedback fires into the exact LangSmith trace record via a pre-assigned run id. Thumbs-down → golden-dataset promotion is manual today — an honest gap, not automated. Loop back to stage 1." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="86" width="290" x="50" y="1042" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e1" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e2" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e3" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s4">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e4" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s5">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e5" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s6">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e6" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s7">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e7" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s7" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s8">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e8" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s8" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s9">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e9" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s9" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" target="p1_s10">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_e10" edge="1" parent="1" source="p1_s10" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontColor=#7e57c2;" target="p1_s1" value="loop">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="20" y="560" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_fr" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS (what it must do)&#xa;&#xa;• Streaming chat — multi-step planning + replan-on-failure + parallel step execution&#xa;• Multi-format document RAG (PDF w/ OCR fallback, DOCX, PPTX, XLSX, XLS, CSV, TXT, MD) with citations&#xa;• NL2SQL stock/fundamentals screener (guarded, read-only)&#xa;• Web search&#xa;• Long-term memory (facts extracted, recalled, user-deletable)&#xa;• Voice input/output&#xa;• Tool calling — market data, portfolio P&amp;L, code interpreter (dev-only), image gen (gated on key), Gmail/Calendar connectors (gated on key), GitHub MCP (read-only)&#xa;• Human-in-the-loop approval for sensitive tools&#xa;• Artifacts (canvas-style documents)&#xa;• Share links&#xa;• Personas&#xa;• Scheduled tasks&#xa;• Daily briefings &amp; price alerts&#xa;• Thumbs up/down feedback wired to trace records" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="400" width="400" x="400" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_nfr" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="NON-FUNCTIONAL TARGETS (real, currently-met gates)&#xa;&#xa;Routing accuracy……gate ≥90% — actual 47/50 = 94.0%&#xa;Injection resistance…gate 100% — actual 76/76&#xa;Plan mechanics………gate 100% — actual 25/25&#xa;RAG retrieval hit-rate…gate ≥90% — actual 15/15 = 100%&#xa;Faithfulness (judge)…gate ≥7/10 — actual 8.2/10&#xa;Backend test coverage…gate 70% — actual ~73-75%&#xa;Cost……………………$0 steady-state marginal cost via free-tier provider chain&#xa;Security………………zero inbound ports on the production server (Cloudflare Tunnel is outbound-only)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="280" width="400" x="400" y="490" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_map" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="HOW THIS MAPS TO THE REAL BUILD (finzorr.ai)&#xa;&#xa;• Orchestration graph = app/orchestration/graph.py (build_graph)&#xa;• Routing/supervisor = app/orchestration/supervisor.py&#xa;• 7 specialists = app/specialists/rag.py, nl2sql.py, tools.py, research.py, general_chat.py, memory.py, web_search.py&#xa;• Infrastructure adapters = app/infrastructure/db, redis, vector_store, llm&#xa;• Domain logic = app/domain/citations.py, pii.py, guard.py, chunking.py, retrieval.py&#xa;• Tool dispatch = app/tools_registry/dispatcher.py&#xa;• API/WebSocket = app/interface/ routers&#xa;&#xa;This is a running production system, not a design exercise — every number below is measured from the live eval suite." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="360" width="430" x="840" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_legend" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="HOW TO READ THIS ATLAS (applies to every page)&#xa;&#xa;■ green box…………LIVE — actually built &amp; running today&#xa;▢ amber dashed……PLANNED — honestly marked gap&#xa;■ blue box……………process / service / reference panel&#xa;■ yellow box…………decision point / routing logic&#xa;■ teal box……………input / entry / user-facing&#xa;■ purple box…………output / synthesis / streamed result&#xa;■ gray box……………dense reference/annotation panel&#xa;■ red box……………risk / warning / incident&#xa;● numbered circle…request-flow order (later pages)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="260" width="430" x="840" y="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_index" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1" value="PAGE INDEX&#xa;&#xa;1  Lifecycle &amp; Requirements (this page)&#xa;2  Discovery, ROI, Capacity &amp; Program Mgmt&#xa;3  Runtime Architecture — 5-Layer Backend (the big one)&#xa;4  Request Flow &amp; Intent Routing (Supervisor)&#xa;5  Memory Architecture&#xa;6  RAG Pipeline Deep-Dive&#xa;7  NL2SQL Screener Pipeline Deep-Dive&#xa;8  Specialists, Tool Calling &amp; Guardrails&#xa;9  Multi-Step Planning Sequence (worked example)&#xa;10 Model / Provider Selection &amp; Benchmarking&#xa;11 Evaluation Suite, Gates &amp; Observability&#xa;12 Deployment, Security &amp; LLMOps (OVH + Cloudflare)&#xa;13 Whiteboard — Transformer &amp; LLM Internals&#xa;14 Operations &amp; Design Playbook&#xa;&#xa;TRANSFORMER DEEP-DIVE SERIES (worked examples)&#xa;15 Tokenization &amp; Embeddings&#xa;16 Positional Encoding &amp; Self-Attention&#xa;17 The Transformer Block in Detail&#xa;18 Decoding &amp; Streaming (Output)&#xa;19 Training Lineage, Stage by Stage&#xa;20 Advanced Concepts (KV Cache, MoE, Quantization…)&#xa;21 Finzorr End-to-End (a real query traced through the code)&#xa;22 Full Pipeline — One-Frame Flow Diagram&#xa;&#xa;INTEGRATIONS&#xa;23 MCP Integrations — GitHub Call Traced + Slack &amp; Friends&#xa;24 Integrations Deep-Dive — Worked Examples (Slack, Drive, Jobs, News)&#xa;&#xa;REVISION&#xa;25 Full Flow — Every Step, One Line Each (Interview Revision)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="470" width="380" x="1310" y="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p1_quote" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="ARCHITECTURE RULE #1&#xa;&#xa;Strict one-directional dependency across the 5-layer backend:&#xa;interface → orchestration → specialists → infrastructure → domain (never the reverse).&#xa;&#xa;app/domain/ is pure business logic — it never imports anything above it. This ordering is what keeps 7 specialists, routing, and checkpointing independently testable." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="200" width="380" x="1310" y="440" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="p2" name="2 . Real Cost Economics, Capacity, Build History &amp; Risk Register">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1220" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p2_t" value="FINZORR.AI — REAL COST ECONOMICS, CAPACITY, BUILD HISTORY &amp; RISK REGISTER. Every figure below is from the actual running system — not a hypothetical enterprise estimate. Green = LIVE today · amber dashed = identified gap, honestly not yet built." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_cost" value="REAL COST ECONOMICS — LLM PROVIDER FALLBACK CHAIN (LIVE, genuine $0 steady-state)&#xa;&#xa;1. Groq — llama-3.3-70b-versatile, primary chat model&#xa;    free tier ≈ 1,000 req/day, $0&#xa;2. Gemini — gemini-2.0-flash, automatic fallback on Groq&#xa;    error/quota, free tier ≈ 1,500 req/day, $0 — also powers&#xa;    image understanding&#xa;3. OpenRouter (optional) — free-tagged models only, $0&#xa;4. Local Ollama (emergency fallback) — llama3.2:3b-instruct-fp16&#xa;    $0 marginal, hardware-amortized&#xa;&#xa;Embeddings: local Ollama nomic-embed-text:v1.5 — $0&#xa;&#xa;Traffic shaping: per-user Redis rate limits + daily per-provider&#xa;token budgets push traffic down this chain before any hard failure.&#xa;&#xa;This is real production traffic at genuine $0 cost — not a projection." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="60" width="560" height="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_cap" value="CAPACITY — REAL PRODUCTION CONTAINER SPECS&#xa;&#xa;api ……………… mem_limit 1.5GB (uvicorn --workers 2)&#xa;postgres ……… 0.7GB&#xa;redis ………… 0.4GB&#xa;qdrant ……… 0.5GB&#xa;ollama ……… 3GB cap — only 2 small local models pulled&#xa;    (the embedder + one emergency chat model)&#xa;cloudflared … 0.1GB&#xa;&#xa;Steady state: roughly 3–4GB total across all containers.&#xa;&#xa;Sizing rule: a 6–8GB VM is comfortable for this footprint —&#xa;no GPU, no autoscaling cluster required for current load." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="60" width="480" height="310" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_legend" value="HOW TO READ THIS PAGE&#xa;&#xa;■ green box…………LIVE — actually built &amp; running today&#xa;▢ amber dashed……PLANNED — honest, identified gap&#xa;■ blue box……………real production reference data&#xa;■ gray box…………dense reference / annotation panel&#xa;■ red box……………risk / incident (real, not hypothetical)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1120" y="60" width="500" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_dev" value="HOW THIS WAS ACTUALLY BUILT&#xa;&#xa;Not a generic 8–10 person team: one developer working&#xa;iteratively with an AI coding agent across many sessions.&#xa;Each hardening wave was independently adversarially&#xa;reviewed before being considered done — the substitute&#xa;used here for a human team code review." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1120" y="220" width="500" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_build" value="REAL BUILD HISTORY — 84 COMMITS, ACTUAL SEQUENCE (not a generic sprint plan)&#xa;&#xa;1. Initial FastAPI + LangGraph + React scaffold&#xa;2. 3-wave ChatGPT-parity build — 20 features, all shipped&#xa;3. Hardening wave — adversarial-review-driven&#xa;4. Grade-10 wave&#xa;5. Agentic-10 wave — real multi-step planning, HITL, parallel Send fan-out&#xa;6. Perfect-10 wave — replanning, parallel execution, memory on pgvector&#xa;    BaseStore, plan evals, api v1, accessibility, load testing&#xa;7. Final-10 wave&#xa;8. LangSmith tracing integration + a completeness audit&#xa;9. RAG hardening wave 1 — document-RAG-router-awareness fix +&#xa;    PPTX/XLSX/XLS support&#xa;10. RAG hardening wave 2 — 12-point RAG Security and Quality Playbook&#xa;11. This session&#39;s own 5-layer modular architecture rewrite —&#xa;    5 sequential waves, each independently verified &amp; adversarially reviewed&#xa;12. Mobile/accessibility fixes&#xa;13. OCR fallback feature&#xa;14. Deployment documentation overhaul" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="390" width="900" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_golive" value="GO-LIVE CHECKLIST — REAL STATUS&#xa;&#xa;Eval suite green ……………………………… DONE&#xa;Load test ……………………………………… DONE — 23,816 requests recorded,&#xa;    0 errors, all non-LLM p95 under 250ms&#xa;Security review ……………………………… DONE — SECURITY_REVIEW.md, full&#xa;    OWASP LLM Top 10 disposition&#xa;Automated nightly backups ……… NOT YET BUILT — open gap;&#xa;    manual pg_dump is the stopgap&#xa;Observability …………………………………… DONE — LangSmith tracing +&#xa;    drift_watch.py + trace_health_watch.py&#xa;Rollback tested ……………………………… DONE — deploy.sh with a tag&#xa;    argument, under 5 minutes&#xa;Cost alerts …………………………………… PARTIAL — ai.budget.exceeded log&#xa;    line exists, no automated alert yet, manual log-watching only" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="960" y="390" width="660" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_risk" value="RISK REGISTER — REAL FINZORR INCIDENTS (likelihood × impact → real fix actually applied, not a hypothetical mitigation)&#xa;&#xa;1. Disk exhaustion on first production build ……… L×H → root cause: an unnecessary build-essential C toolchain (336MB) baked into the image → removed&#xa;2. Missing EMBED_OLLAMA_URL / OLLAMA_URL ……… M×M → a localhost-vs-Docker-service-name networking footgun → fixed by pointing both at the correct Docker service hostnames&#xa;3. Checkpointer cross-worker deadlock ……… L×H → an asyncio.Lock gave zero protection across separate --workers 2 processes, plus CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY needed autocommit=True → both fixed via a one-off single-process setup step&#xa;4. Non-root container could not write to /app ……… M×H → a Docker WORKDIR-before-COPY-chown ordering bug, broke uploads → fixed the ordering&#xa;5. CI pipeline buildx cache-driver break ……… L×H → silently broken until it blocked two real deploys → fixed the cache driver config&#xa;6. Self-hosted GitHub Actions runner silently going unregistered ……… M×H → queued deploys wait forever with zero error surfaced → NOT YET FIXED at the infra level; worked around with a manual emergency deploy&#xa;7. Uploaded files lost on every container restart while their search-index entries survived ……… M×H → silently broke citations → fixed with a persistent volume&#xa;8. Two separate Google OAuth origin_mismatch failures ……… M×M → apex domain and www subdomain are separate origins to Google → fixed by registering both origins" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="790" width="1580" height="380" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="p3" name="3 . Enterprise Runtime Architecture">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1260" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p3_t" value="ENTERPRISE RUNTIME ARCHITECTURE — finzorr.ai&#39;s real 5-layer backend plus production deployment, as one numbered end-to-end request flow. Spine top→bottom = one request. Green = LIVE · yellow = routing · purple = streamed output." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_user" value="User — React SPA (Vite, Tailwind)&#xa;Streaming chat over WebSocket · route badges · citations · thumbs up/down" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="345" y="60" width="520" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_n1" value="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#202124;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="8" y="75" width="26" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_pages" value="Cloudflare Pages&#xa;Serves the static frontend at finzorr.ai and www.finzorr.ai" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="150" width="520" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p3_tunnel" value="Cloudflare Tunnel&#xa;Strictly outbound from the server, zero inbound ports — connects api.finzorr.ai to the api container. The ONLY door to the server." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="150" width="520" height="70" as="geometry" />
