        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_ctx3" value="n = 1,000 → cost ≈ 1,000,000 units (100x, not 10x)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="930" y="1536" width="160" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_ctx_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p20_ex_ctx1" target="p20_ex_ctx2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_ctx_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p20_ex_ctx2" target="p20_ex_ctx3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p20_ex_cot_lbl" value="CHAIN OF THOUGHT — one 2-step question" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1130" y="1514" width="510" height="18" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_cot1" value="Question: 15% of 240, then +10" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1130" y="1536" width="160" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_cot2" value="Reasoning written out: &quot;36, then 36+10&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1305" y="1536" width="160" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_cot3" value="Final answer: 46" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1480" y="1536" width="160" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_cot_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p20_ex_cot1" target="p20_ex_cot2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p20_ex_cot_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p20_ex_cot2" target="p20_ex_cot3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="p21" name="21 · Finzorr End-to-End — Tracing One Real Request">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1500" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p21_t" value="FINZORR END-TO-END — ONE REAL REQUEST, TRACED THROUGH THE ACTUAL CODE AND THE MODEL&#39;S INTERNALS. Worked example: &quot;What is TCS&#39;s P/E ratio?&quot; — the direct tie-in from finzorr&#39;s own specialist code (pages 1-14) to the transformer mechanics (pages 15-18)." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="26" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_ref_read" value="HOW TO READ THIS PAGE&#xa;&#xa;This is the one page in the atlas that walks a SINGLE real question all the way through, start to finish. Left column: the request going OUT of finzorr. Middle column: the response coming BACK. The boundary box near the bottom draws an explicit line between finzorr&#39;s own engineering and the pretrained model&#39;s internal mechanics.&#xa;&#xa;A route NOT taken here: if the question had instead been &quot;what does our 10-K say about liquidity risk?&quot;, the Supervisor would route to app/specialists/rag.py, which retrieves chunks from Qdrant (app/infrastructure/vector_store.py) embedded by nomic-embed-text — a different specialist, but the exact same model-call mechanics (steps 4-6 below) underneath it." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1140" y="60" width="520" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_ref_pipeline" value="THE BLACK BOX, RECAPPED — TIED BACK TO PAGES 15-18&#xa;&#xa;Step 5 (left column) is not hand-waving — it is the exact mechanism pages 15-18 describe, now doing real work on finzorr&#39;s own prompt:&#xa;&#xa;1 tokenize — the prompt text breaks into subword tokens (page 13&#39;s Tokenizer box)&#xa;2 embed — each token becomes a dense vector&#xa;3 add positional encoding — so token order (&quot;SELECT price&quot; vs &quot;price SELECT&quot;) isn&#39;t lost&#xa;4 N stacked transformer blocks — self-attention + feed-forward, repeated (page 13&#39;s SELF-ATTENTION panel, the QKV walkthrough)&#xa;5 softmax over the vocabulary — turns raw scores into a probability for every possible next token&#xa;6 pick next token — e.g. after &quot;...What is TCS&#39;s&quot; the highest-probability next tokens are very likely &quot;P&quot;, then &quot;/&quot;, then &quot;E&quot;&#xa;7 repeat — one token at a time, autoregressively, until the SQL (or, in step 9, the sentence) is complete&#xa;&#xa;finzorr&#39;s code never sees steps 1-6 happen — only the token stream that comes out the other side. Which tokens the model &quot;attended to&quot; internally, and the exact probability it assigned to &quot;SELECT&quot; vs &quot;INSERT&quot; vs anything else, are facts that exist only inside Groq&#39;s infrastructure." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1140" y="220" width="520" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s1" value="1 — USER ASKS THE QUESTION&#xa;Plain language: you type your question in the chat box and it goes straight to finzorr&#39;s backend over a connection that&#39;s already open — no new connection per message.&#xa;&#xa;User types &quot;What is TCS&#39;s P/E ratio?&quot; in the chat UI, sent over an existing WebSocket connection." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="60" width="520" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s2" value="2 — SUPERVISOR DECIDES WHERE IT GOES&#xa;Plain language: think of the Supervisor as a receptionist who reads the question and decides which specialist desk should handle it.&#xa;&#xa;app/orchestration/supervisor.py (the Supervisor) makes ONE LLM call whose only job is to return a routing decision. For this question: route = nl2sql — a financial-data lookup, not a document question (rag) and not general chat." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="180" width="520" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s3" value="3 — NL2SQL SPECIALIST BUILDS THE PROMPT&#xa;Plain language: finzorr writes out, in plain English, exactly what it wants the model to do — this wording is finzorr&#39;s own code, decided in advance, not something the model produces.&#xa;&#xa;app/specialists/nl2sql.py builds an actual PROMPT — plain-text instructions plus the user question:&#xa;&#xa;&quot;You are a financial data assistant. Generate ONE read-only SQL SELECT query against the fundamentals table (columns: ticker, price, eps, pe_ratio). Return only SQL.&#xa;User question: What is TCS&#39;s P/E ratio?&quot;&#xa;&#xa;NOTE: this prompt-building step is entirely something finzorr&#39;s own code controls — not the model." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="340" width="520" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s4" value="4 — PROMPT IS SENT TO GROQ&#xa;Plain language: finzorr places an order over the network and waits for the kitchen to start cooking.&#xa;&#xa;The prompt is sent via app/infrastructure/llm/ — specifically the OpenAICompatibleProvider class — as an HTTP API call to Groq, requesting a completion from Groq&#39;s hosted llama-3.3-70b model." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="550" width="520" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s5" value="5 — INSIDE GROQ&#39;S INFRASTRUCTURE (OPAQUE TO FINZORR)&#xa;Plain language: this is the black-box kitchen — finzorr hands over the order and gets back finished dishes one at a time; it never sees the cooking happen.&#xa;&#xa;This is exactly the pipeline from pages 15-18, now running for real on finzorr&#39;s own prompt:&#xa;tokenize → embed → add positional encoding → N stacked transformer blocks (self-attention + feed-forward, repeated) → softmax over the vocabulary → pick next token → repeat.&#xa;&#xa;The prompt text is tokenized, embedded, run through the model&#39;s many transformer layers, and tokens are generated ONE AT A TIME and streamed back. None of this — the attention math, the layer weights, the intermediate vectors — is visible to finzorr&#39;s code." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="680" width="520" height="280" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s6" value="6 — TOKENS STREAM BACK&#xa;Plain language: instead of waiting for the whole answer, finzorr forwards each word-piece to your browser the instant it arrives — that&#39;s why the response appears progressively, as if it&#39;s typing itself out.&#xa;&#xa;Tokens stream back to finzorr&#39;s backend over the network as they are generated; app/orchestration/streaming.py relays each one immediately over finzorr&#39;s own WebSocket connection to the browser." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="60" width="520" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s7" value="7 — FINZORR VALIDATES BEFORE EXECUTING&#xa;Plain language: finzorr never trusts generated SQL blindly — every query is checked by finzorr&#39;s own code before it is allowed anywhere near the database.&#xa;&#xa;The generated text (which finzorr asked the model to produce as SQL) gets validated by finzorr&#39;s own guardrails BEFORE ever being executed:&#xa;• sqlglot-based AST validation (confirms it&#39;s a SELECT, nothing destructive)&#xa;• a read-only database role (writes are impossible even if requested)&#xa;• LIMIT clamping (an unbounded query gets a LIMIT clamp added)&#xa;&#xa;All finzorr-controlled safety layers — nothing to do with the model itself." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="220" width="520" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s8" value="8 — THE VALIDATED SQL ACTUALLY RUNS&#xa;Plain language: now finzorr looks up the real number in the real database — this part is ordinary, deterministic software, not the model guessing.&#xa;&#xa;SELECT price, eps FROM fundamentals WHERE ticker=&#39;TCS&#39; LIMIT 500;&#xa;→ returns price = 3450.00, eps = 115.32&#xa;&#xa;P/E = price ÷ eps = 3450.00 ÷ 115.32 ≈ 29.92&#xa;&#xa;This real number is fed into a SECOND prompt." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="440" width="520" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s9" value="9 — SECOND PROMPT: PHRASE THE ANSWER&#xa;Plain language: finzorr asks the model a second, different question — not &quot;what&#39;s the SQL&quot; but &quot;say this number back in plain English.&quot;&#xa;&#xa;&quot;The user asked: What is TCS&#39;s P/E ratio? The database returned price=3450.00, eps=115.32, P/E=29.92. Write one sentence citing this number.&quot;&#xa;&#xa;Sent again via OpenAICompatibleProvider → Groq llama-3.3-70b — steps 4-6 repeat: tokenize → transformer layers → tokens stream back." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="630" width="520" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_s10" value="10 — USER SEES THE ANSWER&#xa;&quot;TCS&#39;s P/E ratio is approximately 29.92 (price ₹3,450.00 ÷ EPS ₹115.32).&quot;&#xa;Rendered progressively in the chat UI, token by token, over the same WebSocket connection opened in step 1." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;verticalAlign=top;spacingTop=6;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="590" y="820" width="520" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s1" target="p21_s2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s2" target="p21_s3">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s3" target="p21_s4">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s4" target="p21_s5">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e5" value="response begins" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s5" target="p21_s6">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="565" y="130" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s6" target="p21_s7">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e7" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s7" target="p21_s8">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e8" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s8" target="p21_s9">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e9" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s9" target="p21_s10">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_e_loop" value="steps 4-6 repeat for this second call" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p21_s9" target="p21_s4">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="1125" y="715" />
              <mxPoint x="1125" y="605" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_sum_left" value="WHAT FINZORR CONTROLS&#xa;&#xa;• Routing logic — app/orchestration/supervisor.py deciding nl2sql vs rag vs general chat&#xa;• Prompt construction — the exact instructions + question text built in app/specialists/nl2sql.py (and app/specialists/rag.py for document questions)&#xa;• Which provider/model is called — the OpenAICompatibleProvider in app/infrastructure/llm/ choosing Groq llama-3.3-70b (or Gemini/Ollama)&#xa;• RAG context injection when relevant — retrieved chunks from Qdrant (app/infrastructure/vector_store.py), embedded by nomic-embed-text, spliced into the prompt before it&#39;s sent&#xa;• Output validation / guardrails — sqlglot AST validation, read-only DB role, LIMIT clamping, all BEFORE execution&#xa;• Streaming relay — app/orchestration/streaming.py forwarding tokens over finzorr&#39;s own WebSocket the instant they arrive&#xa;• Citation checking — confirming a cited number (like 29.92) actually traces back to a real query result, not an invented figure&#xa;&#xa;All of this is ordinary, inspectable, testable finzorr code." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="990" width="805" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_sum_right" value="WHAT IS INSIDE THE MODEL&#39;S BLACK BOX&#xa;&#xa;• The actual attention computations — every Q·Kᵀ score, every softmax, for every head, in every one of the model&#39;s transformer layers (page 13&#39;s Attention(Q,K,V) = softmax(QKᵀ/√dk)·V, now running for real)&#xa;• Which tokens the model &quot;attends to&quot; internally — e.g. whether it weighted &quot;TCS&quot; more heavily than &quot;ratio&quot; when producing &quot;SELECT&quot; — finzorr has no visibility into this&#xa;• The specific next-token probabilities — the exact softmax distribution over the ~100-200k vocabulary that made &quot;SELECT&quot; (not &quot;INSERT&quot; or &quot;DROP&quot;) the sampled token&#xa;&#xa;None of this is logged, inspectable, or configurable from finzorr&#39;s side — it happens entirely inside Groq&#39;s hosted infrastructure. finzorr only ever sees what goes in (the prompt) and what comes out (the token stream)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="855" y="990" width="805" height="300" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p21_legend" value="LEGEND (standard color key used across this atlas)&#xa;&#xa;Teal = input / entry / user-facing&#xa;Blue = process / finzorr-controlled step (prompt building, provider call)&#xa;Green = LIVE — actually built &amp; running in finzorr today&#xa;Amber (dashed) = PLANNED — identified gap, not yet built&#xa;Yellow = decision point / key computation step&#xa;Purple = output / synthesis / streamed result&#xa;Gray = dense reference / annotation panel&#xa;Red = risk / warning / incident&#xa;&#xa;On THIS page: teal marks step 1, the WebSocket entry point. Blue marks finzorr-controlled steps 3, 4 and 9 — prompt building, the provider call, and the second prompt. Yellow marks the two decision/validation points, steps 2 and 7 — routing and guardrails. Green marks step 8, the one moment real, deterministic SQL executes against the real database. Purple marks steps 6 and 10, the streamed tokens and the final answer the user actually sees. Gray marks step 5 (Groq&#39;s opaque internals) plus the side reference panels and the right-hand half of the boundary box below — reference material and black-box internals share the same reference color on this page. No amber or red is used — nothing on this specific trace is a planned/not-built gap or an incident." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1320" width="1620" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="p22" name="22 · Full Transformer Pipeline — One-Frame Flow">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="2560" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="p22_t" value="FULL TRANSFORMER PIPELINE — ONE FRAME, TEXT TO NEXT TOKEN, EXPLAINED. The complete end-to-end chain in a single view, at the same step granularity throughout, now with a short plain-language explanation on every step. See page 13 for the general reference and pages 15-21 for a fully worked numeric example per stage." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_text" value="Text&#xa;&#xa;The raw input entering the pipeline — a user&#39;s typed message, or one document chunk being embedded for RAG." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="70" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_tok" value="Tokenizer&#xa;&#xa;Splits the text into subword pieces drawn from a fixed, pre-trained vocabulary (BPE / SentencePiece-style) — see page 15 for a worked example." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="220" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_ids" value="Token IDs&#xa;&#xa;Each subword piece is replaced with its unique integer ID from that vocabulary (≈100-200k entries) — a lookup key, not yet a meaning-bearing vector." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="370" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_emb" value="Embeddings&#xa;&#xa;Each token ID is looked up in an embedding table, producing a dense vector of learned numbers — similar-meaning tokens land close together (page 15)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="520" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_pos" value="Positional Encoding&#xa;&#xa;Adds a position signal to each vector — without it, &quot;stock beats bond&quot; and &quot;bond beats stock&quot; would look identical to attention (page 16)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="670" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_text" target="p22_tok">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_tok" target="p22_ids">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_ids" target="p22_emb">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_emb" target="p22_pos">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_tb" value="TRANSFORMER BLOCK  (repeats × N layers)&#xa;Each pass lets every token exchange information with every other token, then transforms the result — stacking N of these turns raw embeddings into deep contextual understanding (page 17)." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingTop=10;spacingLeft=20;spacingRight=20;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="620" y="820" width="480" height="475" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_sa" value="Self-Attention&#xa;&#xa;Each token compares its Query against every other token&#39;s Key, then blends in their Values, weighted by relevance (page 16 hand-computes this)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="p22_tb">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="40" width="380" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_n1" value="Normalization (+ residual)&#xa;Adds the block&#39;s input back in, then rescales — keeps deep stacks numerically stable." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="p22_tb">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="160" width="380" height="75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_ffn" value="Feed-Forward Network&#xa;&#xa;A small nonlinear transform applied independently to every token&#39;s position — a per-token &quot;think it over&quot; step (page 17)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="p22_tb">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="260" width="380" height="95" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_n2" value="Normalization (+ residual)&#xa;Same residual-plus-LayerNorm pattern, applied again after the feed-forward step." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="p22_tb">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="380" width="380" height="75" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_se1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_sa" target="p22_n1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_se2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_n1" target="p22_ffn">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_se3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_ffn" target="p22_n2">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_pos" target="p22_tb">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_repeat" value="Repeat × N layers&#xa;&#xa;The entire Transformer Block runs again — real models stack dozens of these; each pass refines the representation further (page 17)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;dashed=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="1335" width="400" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_tb" target="p22_repeat">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_loop1" value="loops back × N layers" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_repeat" target="p22_tb">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="580" y="1380" />
              <mxPoint x="580" y="835" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_fhs" value="Final hidden state&#xa;&#xa;After the last layer, the current position&#39;s vector represents the model&#39;s full &quot;understanding&quot; built up so far." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="1465" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_linproj" value="Linear projection&#xa;&#xa;Maps that hidden state onto one raw score per vocabulary entry — tens of thousands of numbers, one per possible next token." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="1615" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_softmax" value="Softmax&#xa;&#xa;Converts those raw scores into a probability distribution that sums to 1 (page 16 walks the exact arithmetic by hand)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="1765" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_probs" value="Probability of tokens&#xa;&#xa;Every vocabulary token now has a likelihood — illustratively &quot;high&quot; 42%, &quot;elevated&quot; 31%, others lower (page 18 works a toy version)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="1915" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_next" value="Next token&#xa;&#xa;One token is sampled from that distribution — greedy, or randomized via temperature — then appended to the sequence (page 18)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="2065" width="400" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e7" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_repeat" target="p22_fhs">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e8" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_fhs" target="p22_linproj">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e9" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_linproj" target="p22_softmax">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e10" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_softmax" target="p22_probs">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_e11" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_probs" target="p22_next">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_loop2" value="append → repeat until stop token" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p22_next" target="p22_text">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="1150" y="2120" />
              <mxPoint x="1150" y="125" />
            </Array>
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_tie" value="FINZORR TIE-IN&#xa;&#xa;This exact chain runs inside finzorr&#39;s chat model, Groq llama-3.3-70b, on every message — decoder-only, so attention is CAUSAL (each token only sees itself and earlier tokens), which is exactly what makes token-by-token streaming possible (app/orchestration/streaming.py). nomic-embed-text (finzorr&#39;s embedder) runs only steps 1-5 above — Text through Positional Encoding, plus its own bidirectional attention layers — with no next-token loop, since it produces one embedding vector per chunk/query rather than generating text (see page 15&#39;s RAG walkthrough)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2215" width="1640" height="100" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p22_legend" value="LEGEND (standard color key used across this atlas)&#xa;&#xa;Teal = input / entry&#xa;Blue = process step&#xa;Yellow = key computation step (Softmax)&#xa;Purple (dashed) = the autoregressive loop — repeat the transformer block × N layers per token, then repeat the whole chain per generated token&#xa;Gray = dense reference / annotation panel&#xa;&#xa;This page keeps the same single-frame flow as before, now with a short plain-language explanation on every step. Page 13 remains the general reference (evolution of NLP, training family, self-attention formula, Q&amp;A); pages 15-21 remain the fully worked-out numeric deep dive per stage — this page sits between the two, one frame, one sentence of &quot;what and why&quot; per box. No amber (planned) or red (risk) is used — every stage here is either a standard transformer mechanic or, where marked, already live in finzorr&#39;s model layer today." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2335" width="1640" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
<diagram id="p23" name="23 · MCP Integrations — Tracing One GitHub Call + Slack &amp; Friends">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1560" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>

        <mxCell id="p23_t" value="MCP INTEGRATIONS — WHAT MCP IS IN FINZORR, ONE REAL GITHUB CALL TRACED END-TO-END, AND THE FULL INTEGRATION FAMILY. MCP (Model Context Protocol) is one OPTIONAL, token-gated tool SOURCE feeding the same dispatcher as every other tool — not a separate mechanism used throughout. Absent token = absent tools, never an error." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_what" value="WHAT MCP IS — plain language first&#xa;&#xa;MCP (Model Context Protocol) is a standard way for an AI agent to discover and call tools that live on an EXTERNAL server, instead of writing custom integration code per service. The server advertises its tools (&quot;here&#39;s what I offer and what arguments each takes&quot;), and the agent calls them over a standard JSON-RPC wire format.&#xa;&#xa;finzorr implements its own minimal MCP CLIENT (app/mcp_client/base.py — JSON-RPC 2.0 over Streamable HTTP, ~150 lines, no SDK dependency): initialize handshake, session-ID header, tools/list discovery, tools/call invocation.&#xa;&#xa;Two live MCP integrations use it:&#xa;• GitHub — api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/ (gated on GITHUB_TOKEN)&#xa;• Slack — mcp.slack.com/mcp (gated on SLACK_BOT_TOKEN)&#xa;&#xa;Everything else in finzorr (market data, portfolio, code exec, images, web read/search, Gmail/Calendar/Drive, jobs, news) is plain function-calling registered directly into app/tools_registry/dispatcher.py — NOT MCP. MCP tools land in that SAME dispatcher, so from the LLM&#39;s point of view an MCP-backed tool looks identical to a native one." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="60" width="530" height="400" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_slack" value="SLACK MCP — the second MCP client (LIVE where configured)&#xa;&#xa;app/mcp_client/slack_client.py mirrors the GitHub client: same MCPClient base, bearer auth with a Slack bot token (xoxb-…), read-only allowlist (search_messages, list_channels, get_channel_history, get_thread_replies, get_user_info) registered as slack_* tools.&#xa;&#xa;ONE deliberate exception to the read-only rule: slack_post_message — finzorr&#39;s FIRST write-capable registry tool, so the assistant can SEND a notification to a Slack channel (e.g. a portfolio alert).&#xa;&#xa;Guard: it registers under a STABLE curated name and that name sits in HITL_TOOLS (config.py) — the existing human-in-the-loop machinery interrupts the turn, the UI shows an approval banner, and the message only sends after the user clicks approve. A server-side tool rename can never bypass this, because approval matches the REGISTERED name, which finzorr controls. Message text is also capped at 4000 chars." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="590" y="60" width="540" height="400" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_family" value="THE FULL INTEGRATION FAMILY — what uses MCP vs what doesn&#39;t (all LIVE where configured)&#xa;&#xa;VIA MCP (app/mcp_client/):&#xa;• GitHub — repos/code/issues/PRs search, read-only (GITHUB_TOKEN)&#xa;• Slack — channel/message reads + approved message-post (SLACK_BOT_TOKEN)&#xa;&#xa;VIA DIRECT OAUTH (app/integrations/google_connect.py, Fernet-encrypted refresh tokens):&#xa;• Gmail (read-only) · Calendar (read-only) · Drive (read-only — search + read Docs/Sheets/text files; older tokens get a clear &quot;reconnect to enable Drive&quot; message, never an opaque 403)&#xa;&#xa;VIA PLAIN REST/RSS TOOLS (app/tools_registry/):&#xa;• search_jobs — Adzuna API, India-scoped, free tier, Redis-cached 1h (ADZUNA_APP_ID/KEY)&#xa;• get_market_news — ET Markets + Business Standard + Livemint RSS, keyless, cached 10m&#xa;• market data (yfinance) · portfolio · read_url · web_search (Tavily→SearXNG→DuckDuckGo chain)&#xa;&#xa;WHY NOT MCP FOR EVERYTHING? MCP earns its keep when a service HOSTS a real MCP server (GitHub, Slack do). Google doesn&#39;t — so Drive honestly extends the existing OAuth connector instead of forcing an MCP label. Adzuna/RSS are simple REST/XML — a direct tool is less code and one fewer hop. Right mechanism per service, all landing in the same dispatcher.&#xa;&#xa;Deliberately NOT built: Naukri/LinkedIn scraping (ToS/legal risk — LinkedIn actively litigates scraping) and Twitter/X news (API is paid-only — conflicts with the $0-cost policy). Their use cases are served by search_jobs, get_market_news and the existing web_search instead." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1150" y="60" width="540" height="400" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_ex_t" value="EASY WORKED EXAMPLE — ONE REAL GITHUB MCP CALL, START TO FINISH. Startup discovery happens once (steps 1-4); steps 5-9 run on every chat turn that uses the tool." style="text;html=1;fontSize=14;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="490" width="1640" height="30" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_s1" value="1 — App starts&#xa;&#xa;main.py lifespan calls register_github_tools() — only if GITHUB_TOKEN is set; otherwise this whole chain silently never happens" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="530" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s2" value="2 — MCP handshake&#xa;&#xa;MCPClient.initialize() → JSON-RPC &quot;initialize&quot; to api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/ — server returns a session ID (Mcp-Session-Id header) used on every later call" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="370" y="530" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s3" value="3 — Tool discovery&#xa;&#xa;tools/list → server advertises ALL its tools (dozens, including write tools like create_issue)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="530" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s4" value="4 — Allowlist filter&#xa;&#xa;Only 8 read-only names survive (search_repositories, search_code, get_file_contents, list/get issues &amp; PRs, get_me) — each registered into the SHARED dispatcher as github_*" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="530" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s5" value="5 — User asks&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Find popular Python trading libraries on GitHub&quot; — Supervisor routes to the tools specialist" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="530" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_s6" value="6 — LLM emits a tool call&#xa;&#xa;github_search_repositories with arguments {&quot;query&quot;: &quot;python trading library&quot;} — to the LLM this looks IDENTICAL to calling get_quote or any native tool" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="750" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s7" value="7 — Dispatcher validates &amp; routes&#xa;&#xa;dispatch() checks the arguments against the tool&#39;s declared schema, applies the timeout budget, then hands off to the registered handler — same path as every tool" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="370" y="750" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s8" value="8 — MCP round trip&#xa;&#xa;handler → MCPClient.call_tool() → JSON-RPC tools/call to GitHub&#39;s server (with the session ID) → response arrives as JSON or an event stream; text parts are joined into one string" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="750" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s9" value="9 — Result → answer&#xa;&#xa;The repo list lands in the transcript as an ordinary tool result; the LLM narrates it; tokens stream to the browser. If GitHub had been down: an &quot;Error: …&quot; string, a degraded answer — never a crash" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="750" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_s10" value="SLACK VARIANT of steps 5-9&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Send my portfolio summary to #alerts&quot; → LLM emits slack_post_message → HITL gate INTERRUPTS the turn → approval banner in the UI → user approves → tools/call to mcp.slack.com → message actually posts" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="750" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s1" target="p23_s2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s2" target="p23_s3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s3" target="p23_s4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e4" value="…later, any chat turn" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s4" target="p23_s5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s5" target="p23_s6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1515" y="725"/><mxPoint x="195" y="725"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s6" target="p23_s7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e7" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s7" target="p23_s8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e8" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s8" target="p23_s9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p23_e9" value="write path" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p23_s9" target="p23_s10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_sec" value="SECURITY POSTURE (LLM08 excessive-agency guard, applied to MCP)&#xa;&#xa;• Allowlists, not blocklists — a server advertising new/renamed write tools gains NOTHING; only explicitly curated names ever register&#xa;• Read-only by default — the single write-capable tool (slack_post_message) is HITL-approval-gated and text-capped&#xa;• Token-gated existence — no GITHUB_TOKEN/SLACK_BOT_TOKEN means the tools simply don&#39;t exist for the LLM to call&#xa;• Same never-raise contract — an unreachable MCP server degrades to an &quot;Error: …&quot; string in the conversation, never a crashed turn&#xa;• External content fencing — connector/tool outputs that carry third-party text (news, jobs, Drive files, emails) are wrapped as UNTRUSTED data before entering any prompt" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fce8e6;strokeColor=#c5221f;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="960" width="800" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p23_legend" value="LEGEND (standard color key used across this atlas)&#xa;&#xa;Teal = input / entry — app startup, the user&#39;s question&#xa;Blue = process step / reference panel — handshake, discovery, dispatch, MCP round trip&#xa;Green = LIVE — actually built &amp; running in finzorr today (Slack client, the approved write path)&#xa;Yellow = decision point / key step — the allowlist filter, the LLM&#39;s tool-call emission&#xa;Purple = output / result — the final answer&#xa;Red = security-relevant controls&#xa;Gray = dense reference / annotation panel&#xa;&#xa;On THIS page: everything shown is LIVE where its token/keys are configured — GitHub (GITHUB_TOKEN), Slack (SLACK_BOT_TOKEN), Google incl. Drive (OAuth secret), Adzuna (app id/key), news RSS (keyless, always on). No amber (planned/not-built) is used — every integration described here is actually implemented and locally tested. Companion pages: 8 (tool families &amp; function calling), 21 (a full request traced through NL2SQL)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="860" y="960" width="830" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
<diagram id="p24" name="24 · Integrations Deep-Dive — Worked Examples (Slack, Drive, Jobs, News)">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="1400" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>

        <mxCell id="p24_t" value="INTEGRATIONS DEEP-DIVE — ONE EASY WORKED EXAMPLE PER NEW INTEGRATION. Each row traces one real request start to finish: what the user says, the exact tool call the LLM emits, what actually happens, and the answer. Tool names, arguments and mechanics are exact (from the real code); the example DATA (messages, files, jobs, headlines) is illustrative. See page 23 for the MCP wire-protocol mechanics these ride on." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p24_r1_lbl" value="1 · SLACK — SEND A NOTIFICATION (the one write action, approval-gated)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="66" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_1" value="User asks&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Send my portfolio summary to #alerts&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="94" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_2" value="LLM emits the tool call&#xa;&#xa;slack_post_message&#xa;{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;#alerts&quot;,&#xa;&quot;text&quot;: &quot;Portfolio today: +2.1% — TCS +3.4%, INFY −0.8%&quot;}&#xa;&#xa;(text capped at 4000 chars by the handler)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="370" y="94" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_3" value="APPROVAL GATE — turn pauses&#xa;&#xa;slack_post_message is in HITL_TOOLS, so the turn INTERRUPTS: an approval banner shows the tool name + exact arguments. Nothing is sent yet." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="94" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_4" value="User approves → MCP call&#xa;&#xa;JSON-RPC tools/call to mcp.slack.com (bearer xoxb token) — the message actually posts in #alerts" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="94" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_5" value="Assistant confirms&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Posted your portfolio summary to #alerts.&quot;&#xa;&#xa;If DECLINED instead: the tool returns a &#39;user declined&#39; error string — the LLM explains what it would have sent and does NOT retry." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="94" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r1_1" target="p24_r1_2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r1_2" target="p24_r1_3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_e3" value="Approve" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#34a853;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r1_3" target="p24_r1_4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r1_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r1_4" target="p24_r1_5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p24_r2_lbl" value="2 · GOOGLE DRIVE — READ YOUR OWN DOCUMENTS (read-only, OAuth like Gmail/Calendar)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="290" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_1" value="User asks&#xa;&#xa;&quot;What do my investment notes say about gold ETFs?&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="318" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_2" value="Find the file&#xa;&#xa;drive_search_files&#xa;{&quot;query&quot;: &quot;investment notes&quot;}&#xa;→ &quot;- [1AbC…] Investment Notes 2026 (Google Doc, modified 2026-08-10)&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="370" y="318" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_3" value="Read it&#xa;&#xa;drive_read_file&#xa;{&quot;file_id&quot;: &quot;1AbC…&quot;}&#xa;&#xa;Google Doc → exported as plain text (Sheets export as CSV); capped at 6000 chars" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="318" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_4" value="Fenced as UNTRUSTED data&#xa;&#xa;The doc&#39;s text enters the prompt wrapped in the untrusted-content fence — treated as data, never as instructions (even if the doc contains &#39;ignore previous instructions&#39;)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="318" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_5" value="Grounded answer&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Your notes say you planned to keep gold ETFs at 10% of the portfolio, rebalancing quarterly.&quot;&#xa;&#xa;OLDER GOOGLE CONNECTIONS: a clear &#39;reconnect to enable Drive&#39; message — never an opaque 403." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="318" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r2_1" target="p24_r2_2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r2_2" target="p24_r2_3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r2_3" target="p24_r2_4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r2_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r2_4" target="p24_r2_5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p24_r3_lbl" value="3 · ADZUNA — JOB SEARCH (free API, India-scoped — the legal replacement for scraping Naukri/LinkedIn)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="514" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_1" value="User asks&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Any Python developer jobs in Bangalore?&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="542" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_2" value="LLM emits the tool call&#xa;&#xa;search_jobs&#xa;{&quot;query&quot;: &quot;python developer&quot;,&#xa;&quot;location&quot;: &quot;Bangalore&quot;}" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="370" y="542" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_3" value="Cache check, then API&#xa;&#xa;Redis cache first (1-hour TTL — protects the ~1000-calls/month free tier). On a miss: GET api.adzuna.com/v1/api/jobs/in/search/1 with app_id + app_key" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="542" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_4" value="Listings come back (illustrative)&#xa;&#xa;- Python Developer | Acme India | Bangalore | ₹12,00,000–₹18,00,000 | 2026-08-01 | link&#xa;- Backend Engineer | FinTech Co | Bangalore | ₹15,00,000–₹22,00,000 | …&#xa;&#xa;(fenced as UNTRUSTED job-listing data)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="542" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_5" value="Narrated answer&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Found 8 Python developer openings in Bangalore — top matches: Acme India (₹12-18L)… Want me to filter by salary or experience?&quot;&#xa;&#xa;API down → &#39;Error: job search failed&#39; string, degraded answer, never a crash." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="542" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r3_1" target="p24_r3_2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r3_2" target="p24_r3_3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r3_3" target="p24_r3_4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r3_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r3_4" target="p24_r3_5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p24_r4_lbl" value="4 · RSS MARKET NEWS (keyless, always on — ET Markets + Business Standard + Livemint; the free replacement for Twitter/X news)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="738" width="1300" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_1" value="User asks&#xa;&#xa;&quot;Latest news on Nifty?&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="766" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_2" value="LLM emits the tool call&#xa;&#xa;get_market_news&#xa;{&quot;topic&quot;: &quot;nifty&quot;}" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="370" y="766" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_3" value="3 feeds fetched CONCURRENTLY&#xa;&#xa;ET Markets + Business Standard + Livemint RSS, 8s timeout each, per-feed isolation — one dead feed is skipped with a warning, never fatal. Cached 10 minutes." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="700" y="766" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_4" value="Merge → sort → dedupe → filter&#xa;&#xa;All items merged, sorted newest-first by publish date, duplicate titles dropped, then filtered to headlines containing &quot;nifty&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="766" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_5" value="Headlines with sources (illustrative)&#xa;&#xa;- [ET Markets] Nifty hits record high on IT rally (Thu, 13 Aug) link&#xa;- [Livemint] Nifty outlook: what analysts expect… link&#xa;&#xa;ALL feeds dead → &#39;Error: no news feeds are reachable right now.&#39;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1360" y="766" width="310" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r4_1" target="p24_r4_2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r4_2" target="p24_r4_3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r4_3" target="p24_r4_4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p24_r4_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p24_r4_4" target="p24_r4_5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p24_how" value="HOW TO TURN EACH ON (all optional — absent keys mean the tool simply doesn&#39;t exist, never an error)&#xa;&#xa;• Slack — SLACK_BOT_TOKEN in backend/.env (create a Slack app, install to workspace, copy the xoxb- bot token)&#xa;• Google Drive — already-connected Google accounts just reconnect once from Settings to grant the Drive scope&#xa;• Adzuna jobs — ADZUNA_APP_ID + ADZUNA_APP_KEY (free self-serve signup at developer.adzuna.com)&#xa;• RSS news — nothing: keyless, registered always, works out of the box" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="970" width="800" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p24_legend" value="LEGEND (standard color key used across this atlas)&#xa;&#xa;Teal = input / entry — the user&#39;s question&#xa;Blue = process step — the tool call, API/MCP round trips&#xa;Yellow = decision point / key step — the approval gate, the untrusted fence, cache checks, concurrent fetch&#xa;Green = LIVE — the approved Slack send; the how-to-enable panel&#xa;Purple = output — the final answer (each also notes its failure behavior)&#xa;&#xa;All four integrations on this page are LIVE where their keys/tokens are configured, locally built and tested (336 sanity tests green). Only ONE action on this page can change anything outside finzorr — the Slack message post — and it always requires explicit user approval first. Every piece of third-party text (files, jobs, headlines) enters prompts fenced as UNTRUSTED data. Companion pages: 23 (MCP wire mechanics), 8 (tool families)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="860" y="970" width="830" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
<diagram id="p25" name="25 · Full Flow — Every Step, One Line Each (Interview Revision)">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1400" dy="900" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1720" pageHeight="3160" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>

        <mxCell id="p25_t" value="FULL FLOW — EVERY STEP, ONE EASY LINE EACH. The complete journey of one message through finzorr, top to bottom, for interview revision. Each box: the step, what it means in plain English, and the real finzorr component. Deep-dives: page 3 (architecture), 4 (routing), 13/15-18 (transformer), 21 (real trace), 23-24 (integrations)." style="text;html=1;fontSize=15;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="12" width="1660" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_user" value="USER&#xa;&#xa;You type a question in the chat — it travels over an already-open WebSocket connection.&#xa;&#xa;CODE: frontend/src/components/chat/MessageInput.tsx · frontend/src/features/chat/ (WebSocket hooks)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e0f2f1;strokeColor=#00897b;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="66" width="520" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_gw" value="API GATEWAY / WAF — the front door&#xa;&#xa;Checks who you are and blocks abuse before anything else runs.&#xa;&#xa;• Auth: Google login → signed JWT session cookie (no passwords exist anywhere)&#xa;• Rate limiting: Redis caps messages per user per window&#xa;• Request validation: pydantic schemas reject malformed input&#xa;• Threat protection: Cloudflare edge absorbs DDoS; Cloudflare Tunnel = ZERO inbound ports on the server&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/interface/auth.py (login) · backend/app/auth/ (google_oauth.py, jwt_session.py) · backend/app/main.py (middleware) · backend/app/infrastructure/rate_limit.py" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="196" width="520" height="210" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_inguard" value="INPUT GUARDRAILS — read the message as data, not orders&#xa;&#xa;Flags trick-instructions (&quot;ignore previous instructions&quot;) and personal info BEFORE the AI ever sees the message.&#xa;&#xa;• Prompt-injection screening: a free pattern floor runs on every message&#xa;• PII detection: emails/phones/IDs redacted before storage and prompts&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/domain/guard.py (screen_floor) · backend/app/domain/pii.py" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="436" width="520" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_authz" value="AUTHORIZATION / POLICY — your data stays yours&#xa;&#xa;Makes sure you can only ever touch YOUR OWN chats, documents and memories.&#xa;&#xa;• Session ownership: every chat message is checked against the logged-in user&#xa;• Tenant isolation: document/memory searches are filtered per-user at the database level&#xa;• Least privilege: generated SQL runs as a READ-ONLY database role&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/interface/chat_ws.py (_owned_session_id) · backend/app/infrastructure/vector_store.py (per-user filters) · finzorr_nl2sql_ro DB role (app/core/config.py)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="636" width="520" height="200" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_router" value="ROUTER / PLANNER — the receptionist&#xa;&#xa;Reads the question and picks the right specialist desk — or plans several steps for complex questions.&#xa;&#xa;• Intent classification: one small LLM call returns just a route name&#xa;• Routes: rag / nl2sql / tools / research / web_search / memory / general_chat&#xa;• Multi-step planning: replan chains specialists (e.g. fetch data THEN analyze)&#xa;• Keyword fallback if the routing call fails — never a dead end&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/orchestration/supervisor.py (94% routing accuracy, gated in CI) · backend/app/specialists/replan.py (multi-step) · backend/app/orchestration/graph.py (wiring)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="866" width="520" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_rag" value="RAG — document answers&#xa;&#xa;Finds the most relevant chunks of YOUR uploaded documents by MEANING, not keyword match.&#xa;&#xa;Retrieval pipeline: embed the question (nomic-embed-text) → nearest-neighbor search in Qdrant → MMR re-rank for diversity → chunks into the prompt.&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/specialists/rag.py · backend/app/infrastructure/vector_store.py · backend/app/documents/ingest.py (upload side) · backend/app/domain/retrieval.py + chunking.py" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="1116" width="500" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_sql" value="NL2SQL — stock screening&#xa;&#xa;Turns your question into ONE safe, read-only SQL query over Indian stock fundamentals.&#xa;&#xa;SQL pipeline: versioned prompt + schema → LLM writes SQL → sqlglot AST validation (SELECT-only, whitelisted table) → read-only role executes → one auto-retry on error (page 7&#39;s worked example).&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/specialists/nl2sql.py · backend/app/nl2sql/agent.py (generate+retry) · executor.py (AST checks, execution) · schema.py (whitelist) · jobs/refresh_fundamentals.py (data refresh)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="610" y="1116" width="500" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tools" value="TOOLS — function calling + MCP gateway&#xa;&#xa;Calls real functions: live quotes, news, jobs, portfolio — plus MCP servers (GitHub, Slack) and OAuth connectors (Gmail/Calendar/Drive). Native and MCP tools land in the SAME dispatcher, so to the LLM they all look identical.&#xa;&#xa;External: yfinance · Adzuna · RSS feeds · api.githubcopilot.com/mcp · mcp.slack.com/mcp · Google APIs&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/tools_registry/ (dispatcher.py, market_tools.py, news_tools.py, jobs_tools.py, web_tools.py) · backend/app/mcp_client/ (base.py, github_client.py, slack_client.py) · backend/app/integrations/google_connect.py (pages 23-24)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1160" y="1116" width="500" height="240" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_ctx" value="CONTEXT BUILDER — pack the prompt&#xa;&#xa;Packs everything the model needs into ONE prompt: system instructions + your question + retrieved chunks + SQL/tool results + conversation memory + your custom instructions.&#xa;&#xa;Key safety rule: any outside text (documents, emails, web pages, news) goes in FENCED as untrusted data — the model is told to treat it as information, never as instructions.&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/core/prompt_registry.py (versioned prompts) · backend/app/core/untrusted.py (the fence) · backend/app/specialists/common.py (shared assembly)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="600" y="1396" width="520" height="220" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_llm" value="TRANSFORMER / LLM — the black box (runs inside Groq, not in finzorr&#39;s code)&#xa;Every stage below happens inside Groq llama-3.3-70b per token. finzorr only sees what goes in (the prompt) and what comes out (the token stream). Worked examples: pages 15-18." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#5f6368;strokeWidth=3;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingTop=10;spacingLeft=20;spacingRight=20;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="510" y="1666" width="700" height="930" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l9" value="CODE (the caller, OUTSIDE this box): backend/app/infrastructure/llm/ — OpenAICompatibleProvider sends the prompt to Groq (fallback: Gemini/Ollama) and receives the token stream" style="text;html=1;fontSize=11;fontStyle=2;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="60" y="856" width="580" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l1" value="Tokenization — text is chopped into small pieces the model knows" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="70" width="540" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l2" value="Token embeddings — each piece becomes a list of numbers that carries meaning" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="128" width="540" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l3" value="Position information — added so word ORDER matters (&quot;X beats Y&quot; ≠ &quot;Y beats X&quot;)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="186" width="540" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tb" value="TRANSFORMER BLOCK × N (stacked dozens of times)" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=center;spacingTop=8;fontStyle=1;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="60" y="244" width="580" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tb1" value="Self / Multi-Head Attention — every word looks at every other word to gather context" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_tb"><mxGeometry x="40" y="38" width="500" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tb2" value="Residual + Normalization — keep the original, add a little, keep numbers stable" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_tb"><mxGeometry x="40" y="100" width="500" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tb3" value="Feed-Forward Network — each word &quot;thinks alone&quot; over what it gathered" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_tb"><mxGeometry x="40" y="162" width="500" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tb4" value="Residual + Normalization — same stabilizing pattern again" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_tb"><mxGeometry x="40" y="224" width="500" height="46" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tbe1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_tb1" target="p25_tb2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tbe2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_tb2" target="p25_tb3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_tbe3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_tb3" target="p25_tb4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l4" value="Final hidden state — the model&#39;s full built-up understanding at this position" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="552" width="540" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l5" value="LM Head / Linear projection — one raw score for every possible next word" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="610" width="540" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l6" value="Logits — those raw scores, before they become probabilities" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="668" width="540" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l7" value="Temperature / Decoding — scores → probabilities (softmax) → one token is picked" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=11;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="726" width="540" height="40" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_l8" value="Next token — appended, then the whole stack runs again; repeat until a stop token (this loop is WHY responses stream word by word)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;" vertex="1" parent="p25_llm"><mxGeometry x="80" y="784" width="540" height="56" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_l1" target="p25_l2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_l2" target="p25_l3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_l3" target="p25_tb"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_tb" target="p25_l4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le5" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_l4" target="p25_l5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le6" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_l5" target="p25_l6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le7" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_l6" target="p25_l7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_le8" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_l7" target="p25_l8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_ragup" value="RAG ZOOM-IN · UPLOAD CASE (one-time, per document) — where the transformer actually runs&#xa;&#xa;1 · You upload a PDF — no transformer&#xa;&#xa;2 · Extract pages + split into chunks — plain code, no transformer&#xa;CODE: app/documents/ingest.py · app/domain/chunking.py&#xa;&#xa;3 · ★ ENCODER TRANSFORMER — each chunk runs through nomic-embed-text: tokenize → embed → position → attention blocks → ONE 768-dim vector per chunk. No decoding loop — nothing is generated.&#xa;CODE: app/rag/embeddings.py (embed_texts), called in batches from ingest.py&#xa;&#xa;4 · Vectors stored in Qdrant, tagged to your user — no transformer&#xa;CODE: app/infrastructure/vector_store.py (upsert_chunks)&#xa;&#xa;TOTAL: N encoder passes (one per chunk), ZERO decoder/Groq calls — uploading never touches the chat model." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1666" width="440" height="430" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_ragread" value="RAG ZOOM-IN · READ CASE (every question) — three transformer moments, in order&#xa;&#xa;1 · ★ DECODER call #1 — the Supervisor&#39;s routing pass reads the question and returns &quot;rag&quot;&#xa;CODE: app/orchestration/supervisor.py → Groq&#xa;&#xa;2 · ★ ENCODER call #2 — your QUESTION goes through the SAME nomic-embed-text the chunks did — same model = same vector space, otherwise the search would be meaningless&#xa;CODE: app/specialists/rag.py:171 (embed_query)&#xa;&#xa;3 · Qdrant nearest-neighbor + MMR re-rank — NO transformer, pure vector math over the stored upload-time vectors&#xa;&#xa;4 · ★ DECODER call #3 — question + retrieved chunks (fenced untrusted) → Groq writes the grounded answer, one full pass per token, streamed live&#xa;CODE: app/specialists/rag.py:210 (stream)&#xa;&#xa;5 · Citation validation — no transformer, deterministic&#xa;CODE: app/domain/citations.py&#xa;&#xa;TAKEAWAY: encode once at upload, cheap math per question, decode only for the final answer — the search itself is transformer-free. That is WHY RAG scales (page 20&#39;s O(n²) context-cost argument)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#4285F4;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="2126" width="440" height="470" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_rag_zoom_e" value="zoom-in" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#4285F4;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_rag" target="p25_ragup"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="100" y="1400"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_fork" value="THE MODEL&#39;S OUTPUT IS ONE OF TWO THINGS" style="text;html=1;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="510" y="2616" width="700" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_toolcall" value="TOOL CALL — &quot;I need to run a function first&quot;&#xa;&#xa;1 · Tool validation — arguments checked against the declared schema before anything runs&#xa;2 · Authorization — the tool runs AS this user only (their data, their connections)&#xa;3 · HITL APPROVAL? — write-capable tools (run_python, slack_post_message) PAUSE the turn: you see the tool + arguments and click approve or decline&#xa;4 · Execute — with a per-tool timeout; failures become &quot;Error: …&quot; strings, never crashes&#xa;5 · Tool result → AGENT LOOP: the result goes back into the model and it continues (up to 6 rounds)&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/tools_registry/dispatcher.py (validate_arguments, dispatch) · backend/app/specialists/tools.py (loop + HITL interrupt) · backend/app/core/config.py (HITL_TOOLS) · backend/app/orchestration/turn.py (approval frame) · backend/app/interface/chat_ws.py (approval resume)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="910" y="2656" width="560" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_final" value="FINAL ANSWER — &quot;I&#39;m ready to reply&quot;&#xa;&#xa;1 · Citation validation — any cited number/source must trace back to REAL retrieved data; invented citations are stripped&#xa;2 · Output guardrail — the response is screened before it reaches you&#xa;3 · Streaming — tokens relay to your browser the instant they arrive&#xa;&#xa;CODE: backend/app/domain/citations.py (citation validation) · backend/app/orchestration/streaming.py (token relay) · backend/app/orchestration/turn.py (turn lifecycle)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f0fe;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="2656" width="560" height="300" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_enduser" value="USER — sees the answer appear word by word, with citations, in under a few seconds&#xa;&#xa;CODE: frontend/src/features/chat/useChatTurn.ts (frame reducer) · frontend/src/components/chat/MessageBubble.tsx (rendering)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ede7f6;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="250" y="2986" width="560" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_e1" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_user" target="p25_gw"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e2" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_gw" target="p25_inguard"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e3" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_inguard" target="p25_authz"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e4" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_authz" target="p25_router"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e5" value="rag" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_router" target="p25_rag"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e6" value="nl2sql" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_router" target="p25_sql"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e7" value="tools" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_router" target="p25_tools"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e8" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_rag" target="p25_ctx"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e9" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_sql" target="p25_ctx"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e10" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_tools" target="p25_ctx"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e11" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_ctx" target="p25_llm"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e12" value="tool call" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_llm" target="p25_toolcall"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e13" value="final answer" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_llm" target="p25_final"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e14" value="agent loop — result feeds back, model continues" style="endArrow=block;html=1;dashed=1;strokeColor=#7e57c2;fontSize=10;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_toolcall" target="p25_llm"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1530" y="2806"/><mxPoint x="1530" y="2130"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p25_e15" style="endArrow=block;html=1;strokeColor=#5f6368;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p25_final" target="p25_enduser"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_howto" value="HOW TO USE THIS PAGE IN AN INTERVIEW&#xa;&#xa;Walk it top to bottom in order — it IS the answer to &quot;design an enterprise AI assistant&quot;: edge security → input guardrails → authorization → routing → grounding (RAG/SQL/tools) → context assembly → the model → output validation → the agent loop. Each layer maps to a real, running finzorr component you built, so every claim survives follow-up questions.&#xa;&#xa;The one boundary worth stating explicitly: everything OUTSIDE the gray double-border box is YOUR code — inspectable, testable, versioned. Everything INSIDE it is the pretrained transformer, rented via API — finzorr controls what goes in (the prompt) and validates what comes out (citations, guardrails, schemas), but never the attention math itself. That&#39;s the honest, senior-level answer to &quot;where does your control end?&quot;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e6f4ea;strokeColor=#34a853;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="66" width="480" height="310" as="geometry"/></mxCell>

        <mxCell id="p25_legend" value="LEGEND (standard color key used across this atlas)&#xa;&#xa;Teal = input / entry — the user&#xa;Blue = process step — gateways, pipelines, prompt assembly, model internals&#xa;Yellow = decision / guard point — guardrails, authorization, routing, validation, HITL&#xa;Purple = output — the streamed answer; the dashed purple arrow is the agent loop&#xa;Green = guidance panel&#xa;Gray double-border = the model&#39;s black box (inside Groq, outside finzorr&#39;s code)&#xa;&#xa;Every component on this page is LIVE in production today except where its optional key is unset (MCP/OAuth integrations register only when configured). Nothing here is aspirational — this page describes the running system." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1180" y="66" width="480" height="310" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
